\ Exactly measured candidate years between signed-wide gate positions.
\ This adds a correct candidate representation at very large absolute
\ day coordinates and gate indices; native year discovery still uses
\ the original 32-bit candidate record and must be migrated later.
\
\ A year is (opening gate, closing gate]; its duration is whole DAYS,
\ not the number of gate spans. At least six positive gate gaps are
\ required, and the day length must lie between 252 and 5778.
\ Since each gap is 42..963 days, also enforce 42*G <= L <= 963*G.
\ These physical inequalities reject inconsistent synthetic endpoints.
\ Ordered candidates compare day length first, then earlier signed-wide
\ opening coordinate. Gate indices never act as a tie-breaker.
\
\ Native signed arithmetic is used only for small constant factors.
\ All positions, differences, span counts and lengths are exact wide.
\ This module has not been compiled or run under CAL.

A wide year candidate has
  a wide signed day called opening day,
  a wide signed day called closing day,
  a wide signed day called opening index,
  a wide signed day called closing index,
  a wide quantity called span count,
  a wide quantity called year length,
  a number called valid.

The first extended candidate is a wide year candidate.
The second extended candidate is a wide year candidate.
The extended year containment result is a number.
The extended year ordering result is a number.

\ Explicit CAL types for scratch signed records and exact-wide year bounds.
The wycdaydelta is a wide signed day.
The wycindexdelta is a wide signed day.
The wycminspans is a wide quantity.
The wycmindays is a wide quantity.
The wycmaxdays is a wide quantity.
The wycshortdays is a wide quantity.
The wyclongdays is a wide quantity.

To measure a wide year candidate:
  Put 0 into the wide year candidate's valid.
  Put "0" into the wide year candidate's year length.
  Put "0" into the wide year candidate's span count.
  Put the wide year candidate's closing day into the wycdaydelta.
  Subtract the wide year candidate's opening day from the wycdaydelta.
  If the wycdaydelta's polarity is not 1, exit.
  Put the wycdaydelta's absolute quantity into the wide year candidate's year length.
  Put the wide year candidate's closing index into the wycindexdelta.
  Subtract the wide year candidate's opening index from the wycindexdelta.
  If the wycindexdelta's polarity is not 1, exit.
  Put the wycindexdelta's absolute quantity into the wide year candidate's span count.
  Verify a wide year length and span count for the wide year candidate.

To verify a wide year length and span count for a wide year candidate:
  Put "6" into the wycminspans.
  If the wide year candidate's span count is numerically smaller than the wycminspans, exit.
  Put "252" into the wycmindays.
  If the wide year candidate's year length is numerically smaller than the wycmindays, exit.
  Put "5778" into the wycmaxdays.
  If the wycmaxdays is numerically smaller than the wide year candidate's year length, exit.
  Put the wide year candidate's span count into the wycshortdays.
  Multiply the wycshortdays by 42.
  If the wide year candidate's year length is numerically smaller than the wycshortdays, exit.
  Put the wide year candidate's span count into the wyclongdays.
  Multiply the wyclongdays by 963.
  If the wyclongdays is numerically smaller than the wide year candidate's year length, exit.
  Put 1 into the wide year candidate's valid.

To evaluate extended year containment given a wide year candidate and a wide signed day:
  Put 0 into the extended year containment result.
  If the wide year candidate's valid is not 1, exit.
  Compare the wide year candidate's closing day with the wide signed day.
  If the signed day precedence result is 1, exit.
  Compare the wide year candidate's opening day with the wide signed day.
  If the signed day precedence result is 1,
    put 1 into the extended year containment result.

To evaluate extended year ordering given a wide year candidate and another wide year candidate:
  Put 0 into the extended year ordering result.
  If the wide year candidate's year length is numerically smaller than the other wide year candidate's year length,
    put 1 into the extended year ordering result; exit.
  If the other wide year candidate's year length is numerically smaller than the wide year candidate's year length, exit.
  Compare the wide year candidate's opening day with the other wide year candidate's opening day.
  If the signed day precedence result is 1,
    put 1 into the extended year ordering result.
